                            "матем. число измерений геометрической фигуры"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc1a7f83-4d60-4bee-807c-2be1164ff919",
                        "source_entry_id": "51be3a85-7159-3f04-be5d-4a4204538f8e",
                        "target_lang_word": "dimension",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dimension",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52424668-8163-358b-b41b-fbc5451eb944",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A single aspect of a given thing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1771cd4d-7e18-4d9c-a68a-310dd4650529",
                                                "sense_id": "52424668-8163-358b-b41b-fbc5451eb944",
                                                "text": "This film can be enjoyed on many dimensions - the script is great, the acting is realistic, and the special effects will simply take you aback."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f8d60e5-7984-3def-b5d4-fb1a00221412",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A measure of spatial extent in a particular direction, such as height, width or breadth, or depth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bdbbde0-d3f3-47c0-8a66-09bdc0ba2df6",
                                                "sense_id": "6f8d60e5-7984-3def-b5d4-fb1a00221412",
                                                "text": "I can tell you that in your universe you move freely in three dimensions that you call space. […] After that it gets a bit complicated, and there's all sort of stuff going on in dimensions thirteen to twenty-two that you really wouldn't want to know about."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96a70645-c36e-40ac-baf1-fd1c4ebf69b1",
                                                "sense_id": "6f8d60e5-7984-3def-b5d4-fb1a00221412",
                                                "text": "We live our lives in three dimensions for our threescore and ten allotted years. Yet every branch of contemporary science, from statistics to cosmology, alludes to processes that operate on scales outside of human experience: the millisecond and the nanometer, the eon and the light-year."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebbf8ccb-9f2f-363b-9813-82345ecb3e76",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A construct whereby objects or individuals can be distinguished."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b50669a-1a09-3a4e-9e74-c2c10e3ab82a",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The number of independent coordinates needed to specify uniquely the location of a point in a space; also, any of such independent coordinates."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81869510-a916-352e-9a9a-4d67a4aaff75",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The number of elements of any basis of a vector space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61f268db-4bc0-3341-ba96-9df3078f6500",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of the physical properties that are regarded as fundamental measures of a physical quantity, such as mass, length and time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "390586ea-c290-48fa-bd46-c67abf6432ff",
                                                "sense_id": "61f268db-4bc0-3341-ba96-9df3078f6500",
                                                "text": "The dimension of velocity is length divided by time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c76314f5-509f-36f6-b81d-7dc1cbbf7dd2",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the independent ranges of indices in a multidimensional array."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "668bdf35-1f2d-3293-9ee4-fd20bfd69d3a",
                                        "entry_id": "825629c1-32a2-35ee-b6e9-59e1fc79cce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A universe or plane of existence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dba95aa8-c221-47c3-ba9d-ce1b7a40ae5d",
                                                "sense_id": "668bdf35-1f2d-3293-9ee4-fd20bfd69d3a",
                                                "text": "a machine that lets you travel to a parallel dimension."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64abfebf-84b0-4327-9529-44406dab0603",
                                                "sense_id": "668bdf35-1f2d-3293-9ee4-fd20bfd69d3a",
                                                "text": "\"If a man should wish to be in some other place, it is entirely possible for him to imagine himself in that place and, diving back through the negative dimension, to emerge out of it in that place with instantaneous rapidity. To imagine oneself———\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88cec147-0e30-4bdb-b90f-e61768d5b708",
                                                "sense_id": "668bdf35-1f2d-3293-9ee4-fd20bfd69d3a",
                                                "text": "DR. PAUL MANHEIM: I have been on the other side. I have touched another dimension. Part of me is still there.\nLAURA MANHEIM: Help him.\nDR. CRUSHER: Try to stay calm Dr. Manheim. I don't think it's going to help you're struggling against it.\nDR. PAUL MANHEIM: My mind is floating between two places. It is difficult to know which is which. There is no way to explain it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f461e1c-d847-414e-ab7a-e37fb1dbff42",
                                                "sense_id": "668bdf35-1f2d-3293-9ee4-fd20bfd69d3a",
                                                "text": "He was experimenting with matter transportation through the nth dimension."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dimension",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b1b0045-97b8-386d-8b33-212e03df2300",
                                        "entry_id": "82b6c9dc-f5d7-3e03-a7a8-570a01cb4bfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mark, cut or shape something to specified dimensions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bfd33b1-6d0a-439e-b77c-3c0e7f62ae2c",
                                                "sense_id": "2b1b0045-97b8-386d-8b33-212e03df2300",
                                                "text": "Nameless and formless the Spirit within shines forth, unconditioned and everlasting. What name is befitting the soul? How shall Infinite Effulgence be manifested? Too great a light blinds the senses. Too great a truth is too exhilarating for the student. The boundless, infinite Sentience, incomprehensibly dimensioned in Being and Intelligence, rests Unseen and Unthinkable in the shore of His Own omnipresent and superomnipresent consciousness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b8108d8-f572-457d-b2f3-4753fc79f588",
                                                "sense_id": "2b1b0045-97b8-386d-8b33-212e03df2300",
                                                "text": "The mechanical drawing artist almost automatically lays down a triangle in order to draw a line in the desired place. Data entry for AutoCAD, by contrast, requires you to think in terms of coordinate positions rather than in the customary patterns of dimensioning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c76dcd1-86ec-4c4e-b28f-f1061bd33b8a",
                                                "sense_id": "2b1b0045-97b8-386d-8b33-212e03df2300",
                                                "text": "Some people muse over real estate listings in the Sunday paper, looking at floor plans for apartments they could never afford, looking at an idea of what their life might be like with a properly dimensioned foyer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c91c0ec4-e756-48bd-9d1e-5cec6f539e08",
                                                "sense_id": "2b1b0045-97b8-386d-8b33-212e03df2300",
                                                "text": "“The shape seems simple,” Bruce Leep said. “But very precise dimensioning is required. It was difficult to figure out how all of these angles come together.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cb3b818-a399-325f-b172-cffc8c589a91",
                                        "entry_id": "82b6c9dc-f5d7-3e03-a7a8-570a01cb4bfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To specify the size of (an array or similar data structure); to allocate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66191fd0-6156-45f4-92d6-b6124734e9ca",
                                                "sense_id": "9cb3b818-a399-325f-b172-cffc8c589a91",
                                                "text": "Dimension an array to hold only as much data as you intend to put into it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29a3a3af-48f0-47ab-a27b-74c6a596bb30",
                        "source_entry_id": "51be3a85-7159-3f04-be5d-4a4204538f8e",
                        "target_lang_word": "dimensionality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dimensionality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e19525b-95ad-3835-9b75-d3152f5a3332",
                                        "entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or characteristic of possessing dimensions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                        "entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The number of dimensions something has."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e66b759f-8648-4bf5-855f-7c122285f2c2",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "That is to say, it is the Analogue of Space, not in the sense in which we formerly regarded Space as the negation of Matter; but in the sense of Infinite Dimensionality, or of Dimensionality in all directions, as a vague generalization from the three spatial dimensions Length, Breadth, and Thickness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38afd2e7-75c5-48e1-97e1-b8a342a5a885",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "This often happens, for example, when a two-dimensional solution is obtained for data whose appropriate dimensionality is higher."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bfee8fb-8ada-4ba6-9d1f-776ec4b2e139",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "Finite Dimensionality of de Rham Cohomology:\nProposition 5.3.1. If the manifold M has a finite good cover, then its cohomology is finite dimensional."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10f00722-7b17-42f7-bbdc-8ba31e7b4c54",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "As well as the low dimensionality of the Bloch electron states, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81059fad-e5f7-4370-ad4e-d2bea64978c6",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "The difficulties in implementing classification algorithms as is, on high volume databases, derives from the increase in the number of records/instances in the database and of attributes/features in each instance (high dimensionality)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c597e9a8-1923-43aa-aacc-aec60dfcd673",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "The programming language does not impose any restrictions on the dimensionality of the arrays."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e6927b5-b0f5-4fae-8ae5-b3edd280e756",
                                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                                "text": "A vector v=(22,38,52,12) defines a four-dimensional space with a point at the stated co-ordinates, and so on to any dimensionality n. Vector spaces of dimensionality greater than three are impossible to visualise directly […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1aeeec6e-bd0f-4efe-9c80-4e2a5fe2a100",
                        "source_entry_id": "51be3a85-7159-3f04-be5d-4a4204538f8e",
                        "target_lang_word": "dimension",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dimension",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e681d2e5-f61b-3059-8c7a-0392a55c1e75",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ec45e4-f4e6-373b-bef2-f23693d041de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Direction d’expansion d’un objet dans l’espace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bf87cce-56de-4994-bc05-9ae6238bdb9b",
                                                "sense_id": "e681d2e5-f61b-3059-8c7a-0392a55c1e75",
                                                "text": "Une droite est de dimension 1, le plan du tableau est de dimension 2, …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c331f01-d12f-4d96-86a3-bcd915f8c525",
                                                "sense_id": "e681d2e5-f61b-3059-8c7a-0392a55c1e75",
                                                "text": "Parmi les forces connues de ce géant des mondes des 4ᵉ et 5ᵉ dimensions se trouvait une substance —BAL— laquelle, mise en mouvement dans une certaine direction sous l’influence d’instruments propulsifs […], « électrocutait » pour ainsi dire toutes les formes de vie animée qu’elle pénétrait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5a5ae27-f346-47a7-a508-8bf22ea136c9",
                                                "sense_id": "e681d2e5-f61b-3059-8c7a-0392a55c1e75",
                                                "text": "Le sens haptique résulte de l’activité simultanée et coordonnée des récepteurs tactiles et kinesthésiques qui fournissent de l’objet une perception unique en trois dimensions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "740fb815-7545-3849-9fc0-5a3dc74efb1e",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ec45e4-f4e6-373b-bef2-f23693d041de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cardinal d’une base d’un espace vectoriel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9db508d5-bf6f-4553-849e-014a05663b7e",
                                                "sense_id": "740fb815-7545-3849-9fc0-5a3dc74efb1e",
                                                "text": "La dimension de l’ensemble des fonctions réelles de variable réelle est transfinie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c3e5b95-0586-3354-a36d-3d77aca1f697",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ec45e4-f4e6-373b-bef2-f23693d041de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mesure d’une chose dans chacune des directions de l’espace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c37b6085-87de-4e4a-a5e3-c18a125dc8bd",
                                                "sense_id": "7c3e5b95-0586-3354-a36d-3d77aca1f697",
                                                "text": "La distinction que l’on fait entre un astéroïde et une planète est purement arbitraire puisque fondée uniquement sur la dimension."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73c21782-967f-43ec-a5ac-1ce97e4aa7ca",
                                                "sense_id": "7c3e5b95-0586-3354-a36d-3d77aca1f697",
                                                "text": "Il a pris toutes les dimensions de ce bâtiment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "441c1f52-1432-3fd9-b3d1-7a2ac1502b09",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ec45e4-f4e6-373b-bef2-f23693d041de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Taille relative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a58f7339-9b93-4f2c-a1fd-88c288fbd214",
                                                "sense_id": "441c1f52-1432-3fd9-b3d1-7a2ac1502b09",
                                                "text": "A la Tène, on n’a trouvé que des pointes de lances et quelques menus objets en fer, alors que les armes ou outils (ciseaux, couteaux, etc.) de cuivre ont déjà des dimensions importantes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5ada56b-543b-4039-b2da-fefc362f3127",
                                                "sense_id": "441c1f52-1432-3fd9-b3d1-7a2ac1502b09",
                                                "text": "Des azalées, des rhododendrons aux dimensions sénégaliennes donnent une note gaie à ce triste parc où les couleurs éclatantes étonnent, où leur taille gigantesque semble lutter de force avec les vieux remparts toujours solides."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd3d7c7d-bda7-3f98-9dd0-8f6b851c87b4",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ec45e4-f4e6-373b-bef2-f23693d041de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Aspect ; portée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8372fd32-981d-4dbb-8abd-ed1c0d489417",
                                                "sense_id": "bd3d7c7d-bda7-3f98-9dd0-8f6b851c87b4",
                                                "text": "Il explique ainsi que si la réglementation du bruit des tondeuses à gazon n'a pas par nature de dimension transnationale, une intervention de l'Union peut tout de même être justifiée conformément à l’exigence de la réalisation du marché intérieur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2fbe656-4dc4-436b-97db-5ef72b336529",
                                                "sense_id": "bd3d7c7d-bda7-3f98-9dd0-8f6b851c87b4",
                                                "text": "S'y ajoute encore une dimension de précaution politique et sociale : éviter une méga-usine, virtuellement difficile à contrôler et qui, en cas de mouvement social pourrait bloquer l'ensemble de l'activité du groupe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "096f574d-a5fa-3bcd-8f59-222cf964d5d5",
                                        "entry_id": "b6ec45e4-f4e6-373b-bef2-f23693d041de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Combinaison d’unités fondamentales dans laquelle on mesure une grandeur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a381d36-c876-4860-9552-3e25b5058dd2",
                                                "sense_id": "096f574d-a5fa-3bcd-8f59-222cf964d5d5",
                                                "text": "La dimension d’une vitesse est une longueur divisée par un temps, c’est à dire des mètres par seconde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
